    "lesson": {
      "title": "Wildfire & fuel treatment",
      "instruction": "Choose tree patches for earlier fuel treatment. Compare both fires, then test whether your firebreak still works in stronger wind.",
      "explanation": "Same ignition, fixed vegetation pattern, wind and moisture in both maps. A fixed central strip has reduced fuel; width is rounded to whole patches. A deterministic downwind heat-spread model illustrates reduced severity and crossing under extreme conditions. Intensity is a relative index, not a real fire forecast. Fire is a natural ecological process in many landscapes. Real prescribed burning requires qualified professionals, an approved plan and suitable conditions."
    },
